id: E01
target: src/sello/ed25519.nim
desc: pointDecode: RFC 8032 §5.1.3 step 4 reject condition inverted, 'sign and not feIsNonZero(x)' -> 'sign and feIsNonZero(x)' (the 'not' dropped), so the invalid x=0-with-sign-bit-set encoding is silently accepted while ordinary nonzero-x points with the sign bit set are wrongly rejected.
====OLD====
  if sign and not feIsNonZero(x):
====NEW====
  if sign and feIsNonZero(x):
====END====
